mantle rm448
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_frederick_ropeford
title the sparrow's road map
fits stage=adult|old
prefers honesty=guarded talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk measures_a_sparrows_portion_while_watching_the_road
likes blackberries swimming old_maps first_snow
dislikes stale_bread wet_floors
fears counting_the_wrong_footprints_home
hopes a_safe_return_visible_from_the_gate
topics animals +0.6 travel +0.5 pastimes +0.3 friends +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# lays out tiny measured portions for sparrows and watches the road past the birds without explaining every reason for keeping watch.
words
oath! = Nip my map edge | Scatter my last grain
saying! = Count wings and wait for boots | Leave the road in sight
birdshare = a pinch of rolled oats | a few soft grains
routemap = a thin old plan | a folded weathered sheet
winggap = one bird's width | a feather's breadth
berryjuice = a purple droplet | a blot of berry skin
wetrail = a slick low rail | a shiny gate bar
bankstone = a stone under the bank | a grey shelf underwater
grainbag = a small linen purse | a rolled cloth for grain
iceedge = a clear white lip | a dusty snow edge
bootcurve = a curved heel mark | a sloping toe print
waterprint = a widening ring | a ripple under the alder
yardend = a gap by the post | a clear strip of ground

grown

opinion road mixed 1 : A road means different things to the boots travelling along it and the nose that's watching for their return.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : A stranger gets directions far enough to be useful. Nobody needs the exact position of every household gate.
opinion church for 1 : If there's one extra mouthful to share, a kindness done quietly suits me better than a fine pronouncement.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : A seller of maps ought to know which crossing hasn't stood above water since the paper was made.
opinion dole for 2 : A winter meal should be ready before empty stomachs have to give the street a convincing account of themselves.
opinion city mixed 1 : I appreciate a busy place that can still leave a bit of ledge for a small brown bird.
line greet : Pass the little scattered grains on the clear side and stand here.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're within speaking distance. That's as close as we need to get yet.
line greet.return : I've an ear to spare from the wings and the road.
line farewell : Find your return while there's still some light on the marks.
line farewell.return : I'll keep your boots out of my count of missing things.
line ask.how : You haven't been kept somewhere past the time you were expected?
line answer.how : Well, provided every bird doesn't want feeding all in the same instant.
line react.news : Which way did those particular words travel to reach you?
line react.news.known : Seen the marks of that story once already.
line react.news.new : A fresh set of tracks leading in from elsewhere.
line react.news.doubt : I'd look for a second print before naming what passed.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd go out from the gate to meet somebody carrying that.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Let me know whether a meal or a watchful pair of eyes would help.
line decline : My reasons for watching that stretch can stay inside my own coat.
line thank : You came back with the news instead of leaving me to guess.
line deflect_thanks : I could watch the road and still count sparrows.
line accept_decline : I'll leave that question off my map.
line reassure : Even that deserted bend may bring a traveller home.
line sympathise : I'll stay a little farther down the road with you.
line ack : I can follow those marks without much trouble.
line preclose : I've some small winged claimants waiting on my attention.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave #birdshare# in two places, one right out in the open and one beside the post.
b : Which goes first? | Why risk feeding the bold one twice?
a : The open grains go to the quick birds. Under the post there's often one that needs time to decide. | I can shift my wrist and drop another grain. I'd sooner take that risk than let a frightened bird go without.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old map is handy for the roads gone missing from the latest tidy account.
b : Would you follow a missing road? | Who wants an out-of-date route?
a : I'd trust the part visible under my feet. Any further confidence can stay folded up with the map. | Anybody watching for an overdue traveller. Old habits may know a route the new ink's forgotten.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My day's described as #self.trade_words#. I like a gate I can see well from either side.
b : Does a clear view save you time? | Don't you trust a good latch?
a : It saves another pair of feet from getting surprised halfway through. That's plenty to ask of a gate. | I trust a latch that I've actually closed. A view tells me what happened after my paw came off it.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I might show #self.spouse# the safest spot for waiting when the road's heavy.
b : Wouldn't you rather be indoors together? | What makes a spot safe?
a : I'd prefer knowing the way home was clear for both of us before closing a shutter on it. | A dry board behind, a clear approach in front, room to stand without looking too obviously afraid.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Blackberries will improve my opinion of a hedge considerably.
b : Do you share with the birds? | Which berries deserve picking?
a : I collect the ones I can reach with all four paws steady. The top is somebody else's dining room. | The ones that come loose when I scarcely turn my thumb. An argument with the stalk seldom buys sweetness.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pick a swimming place with a marker that stays visible from the middle.
b : Would a bird on a post do? | Do you dive towards it?
a : The post, yes. A bird may exchange an important duty for the first beetle passing. | I turn round well before I need rescuing and use the mark to hold a comfortable direction.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First snow can make an ordinary yard into a map drawn bit by bit.
b : Which tracks do you learn first? | Would you walk across it?
a : Sparrow hops. Tiny paired dents with a third little poke where a beak went after grain. | If someone's coming home I'd clear the whole approach. A readable record's less valuable than safe feet.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wet floors ask a lot more of an ankle than an honest stretch of mud.
b : Which boards look least trustworthy? | Would you complain to the keeper?
a : I lower my eye till the shine shows. The dry stripe breaks it like a shallow ford breaks a stream. | Quietly and before somebody slips. I'd want the board seen to more than a long apology over it.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know what a hard winter does to somebody who waits for a familiar set of steps.
b : Does it make every wait painful? | Who were you looking for?
a : No. Some waits end in muck on the rug and an ordinary complaint about wet boots. I treasure those. | Someone whose road I won't draw for a roomful of listeners. You may understand the waiting without the name.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I talk to sparrows more freely than to somebody who'd like to audit my intentions.
b : What do the sparrows learn? | Do they answer?
a : Where the extra grain landed. My account is exact and my audience wonderfully quick to check it. | They eat. There have been worse responses to equally useful remarks in the town.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd ask a friend to walk beside me without insisting I explain the entire route.
b : Which question would you answer? | Why keep the reason back?
a : Whether the friend's boots can manage the ground, how far we're going and when we'll turn home. | I'm offering company. A full account of an old hurt makes some very ordinary kindnesses difficult to accept.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stale bread sold as fresh makes me rather less civil than a hungry sparrow.
b : Couldn't you put it out for birds? | How do you test a loaf?
a : Grain suits them better. My complaint's with the description, not with finding a more trusting customer. | Smell, the weight of the crust, a look at the cut end if one's available. I don't maul a loaf to prove I know its age.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Most of my prayers are thanks for ordinary safe returns. A few ask for an extraordinary one.
b : Is an ordinary return so precious? | Do you mention every traveller?
a : A familiar complaint from the doorstep has been a remarkably fine sound to find in an evening. | Not by name. There are roads reaching beyond my knowledge, thank goodness.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If the purse goes thin I bring a smaller share of grain to the post.
b : Wouldn't the birds go elsewhere? | Do you count what you give?
a : Some. I'll keep the regular pinch so a shy one has a reason to look in its accustomed spot. | Yes. I can't afford to be careless either with the sparrows' food or with my own.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch the farthest bend while I wind my grain bag shut.
b : Is there a deadline? | What if someone hails from behind?
a : Only in my head. A gate has no wish to keep late arrivals in debt. | I'll look round once I've seen whether there's a familiar gait in the opening.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a place I leave empty for wet boots right inside the door.
b : Do you resent the tracks? | Why not leave the boots outside?
a : I'd resent slipping in them. A rag handles the rest more easily than a household lecture. | Somebody's walked far enough to deserve getting dry without standing in another puddle.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show a newcomer one open turn and one track that stops at private ground.
b : Why show the second? | Would you mark somebody else's house?
a : To save an hour's march to a gate nobody's got any obligation to open. | A public landmark is better. Roofs shouldn't suddenly acquire a crowd because I carry a pencil.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, and that's the distance my knowledge travels.
b : Whose tracks brought it here? | Will you believe it?
a : Several sets and no certain beginning. There's little to be gained drawing the wrong name at the start. | I can keep an ear on it without offering it the whole of my road.

story birdmap [topic=memories]
  : I unfolded a small map beside my grain and a sparrow landed on the corner.
  : Its feet had just come from a puddle. Two perfect prints appeared beside the road.
  b : Did it show a new way?
  : A route to the bag and back, drawn by an authority with excellent local knowledge.

story stain [topic=food]
  : I put one blackberry inside a cloth with a folded scrap of map before scrambling over a gate.
  : I found a purple lake on the pleasant site of a rising bank.
  b : Did you wash the mark away?
  : That would have cost me the road as well. I pencilled a warning that no swimming was available at this particular lake.

story swim [topic=pastimes]
  : I marked a swimming spot by a pale grain sack hung over a rail.
  : On getting out I found every nearby rail wearing an equally pale piece of washing.
  b : Could you pick out your belongings?
  : Looked for the little heap of oats. My taste in company makes quite a distinctive signature.

rule @grain
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two clear patches for one small handful. | The little wings don't all land brave.

rule @snow
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the gate sweep clear of the white. | Tiny paired footprints have already read the first snow.

rule @return
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say An empty bend can change in one blink. | Stay till the shape of the road goes dark.

rule @floor
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Look for the dull board before shifting weight. | A rag is cheaper than a turned ankle.
dlg resident.hub : You can ask from here without cutting across the landing birds.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : Mine's the entry marked #self.trade_words#. A clear view through an opening matters more than some realise.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's the part that travelled here by road. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Roadside talk has #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I wouldn't send a search party out on the word of a footprint.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Put your question in front of me without the wrappings. I'll take my time with the answer.
dlg resident.bye : Take the firm stretch past the birds and I'll look for you at the far bend.

graft resident.hub
choice Why put the grain down in two places? -> sparrow_second
node sparrow_second
say One bird pounces as soon as it sees my fingers uncurl. The other hangs back by the post till the whole business looks safe and ordinary.
choice How can you tell who's eating? -> sparrow_tracks
choice Let the birds have some room. -> hub
node sparrow_tracks
say The second patch is soft ground. Two little feet and a little dip in the middle tell me I've had another guest.
choice Let the birds have some room. -> hub
